{title: Savior of the Nations, Come}
{artist: Ambrose of Milan, Martin Luther, tr. William M. Reynolds / Nun komm, der Heiden Heiland}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: Am}
{key_original: Gm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: savior-of-the-nations-come.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Savior_Of_The_Nations_Come-Nun_Komm_Der_Heiden_Heiland)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Sa[Dm]vior [Em]of [C]the [Dm]na[E]tions, [Am]come;
[Am]Virgin’s [Dm]Son, here [G]make [C]Thy home!
[C]Mar[G]vel [C]now, [F]O [Dm]Heaven [E]and [Am]earth,
[F]That [Dm]the [Em]Lord [Am]chose [E]such a [Am]birth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Not [Dm]by [Em]hu[C]man [Dm]flesh [E]and [Am]blood;
[Am]By the [Dm]Spirit [G]of [C]our God
[C]Was [G]the [C]Word [F]of [Dm]God [E]made [Am]flesh,
[F]Wo[Dm]man’s [Em]off[Am]spring, [E]pure and [Am]fresh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Won[Dm]drous [Em]birth! [C]O [Dm]won[E]drous [Am]Child
[Am]Of the [Dm]virgin [G]un[C]defiled!
[C]Though [G]by [C]all [F]the [Dm]world [E]dis[Am]owned,
[F]Still [Dm]to [Em]be [Am]in [E]Heaven en[Am]throned.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]From [Dm]the [Em]Fa[C]ther [Dm]forth [E]He [Am]came
[Am]And re[Dm]turneth [G]to [C]the same,
[C]Cap[G]tive [C]lead[F]ing [Dm]death [E]and [Am]hell
[F]High [Dm]the [Em]song [Am]of [E]triumph [Am]swell!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Am]Thou, [Dm]the [Em]Fa[C]ther’s [Dm]on[E]ly [Am]Son,
[Am]Hast over [Dm]sin the [G]vic[C]tory won.
[C]Bound[G]less [C]shall [F]Thy [Dm]king[E]dom [Am]be;
[F]When [Dm]shall [Em]we [Am]its [E]glories [Am]see?
{end_of_verse}
